 Reservation Workflow
The reservation process follows these steps:
1. User Login
Requester accesses the system
2. Select Facility
Choose an active facility
3. Submit Reservation
Enter purpose, start time, and end time
4. Pending Approval
5. Administrator Reviews Request
Approved
Administrator schedules reservation
Rejected
Rejection reason recorded
6. Facility Staff Starts Usage
Status becomes In Use
7. Reservation Completed
Business Rules
1.	Every user must have a registered account to access the system.
2.	A password must contain at least six characters during registration.
3.	Only Administrators can add facilities.
4.	Only Requesters can submit reservation requests.
5.	Reservations must have a selected facility, purpose, start time, and end time.
6.	Reservation start time must be in the future.
7.	Reservation end time must be later than the start time.
8.	Only Administrators can approve or reject pending reservations.
9.	An Administrator must provide a rejection reason.
10.	Only approved reservations can be scheduled.
11.	Requesters can cancel only their own pending reservations.
12.	Only Facility Staff can update reservations to In Use or Completed.
13.	Only active facilities appear in the reservation selection list.
14.	Users can only access features permitted by their assigned roles.

